    "mechanism": {
      "summary": "÷exp has only 6/60 non-saturated cells. These 6 cells CANCEL OUT the existing rank separation rather than amplifying it.",
      "detail": [
        "stroke_tpa: 120B/35B/20B all have acts < exp (4-6 vs 9). Their scores DROP. But 4B (acts=10 > exp=9) is NOT penalized. Effect: large models lose rank advantage on this scenario.",
        "af/gi/copd: ONLY 4B has acts < exp. 4B loses its CGA-based rank advantage on these 3 scenarios.",
        "NET: Large models are penalized on stroke; 4B is penalized on 3 expansion scenarios. These opposing effects COMPRESS rank sums, reducing chi2."
      ],
      "rank_sum_range": {
        "cga_alone": 13.5,
